cff-version: 1.2.0

title: "vqubit: a dependency-free quantum computing framework for Python, written in V"

message: >-
  If you use vqubit in academic work, please cite it using this file (GitHub
  renders a "Cite this repository" button from it). The software is archived at
  the GitHub tag of the version you used.

abstract: >-
  vqubit is a quantum-computing library for Python whose numerical core is
  written in V and compiled to a native extension. It mirrors Cirq's API —the
  same gates, circuits, simulators, transformers and protocols— while having no
  runtime dependencies: the wheel needs only the standard library and the
  compiled extension. It includes state-vector and density-matrix simulators, a
  stabilizer simulator, a dependency-free OpenQASM 2.0 importer, Quirk and JSON
  serialization, and harnesses that check its behaviour against cirq-core.

